---@class posthog.review_hog.ReviewTriggerError
---@field error string Human-readable explanation of why the trigger was rejected.
---@field code? posthog.review_hog.ReviewRequestRefusalEnum Why the request was refused, for a client that shows its own reason: 'flash_after_full' (the PR already has a published Deep review), 'resolution_not_opted_in' (the PR owner has not turned on resolving comments). Absent for other errors. * `flash_after_full` - Standard after a published Deep review * `resolution_not_opted_in` - The pull request owner has not opted in to resolution

---* `review` - Review
---* `review_only` - Review only
---* `resolve_only` - Resolve only
---* `flash` - Standard
---@alias posthog.review_hog.ReviewTriggerRequestRunModeEnum "review"|"review_only"|"resolve_only"|"flash"

---@class posthog.review_hog.ReviewTriggerResponse
---@field workflow_id string Temporal workflow id for the started review run; empty when no run was started.
---@field status string Run lifecycle marker: 'started' when the review was queued, 'already_reviewed' when the pull request's current commit already has a published review in the requested mode, 'joined_running_review' when a review was already running and the request was queued on that pull request's run, to start after the running turn. A requested Deep review waits for an active Standard review.
---@field repository string The pull request's repository as 'owner/repo'.
---@field pr_number number The pull request number.
---@field head_sha string|distilled.Null The pull request's head commit when the request was accepted.
---@field review_mode posthog.review_hog.ReviewTriggerReviewModeEnum|distilled.Null The review this request runs: 'full' (Deep) or 'flash' (Standard). Null for 'resolve_only', which runs no review. * `full` - Deep * `flash` - Standard
---@field report_id string|distilled.Null Id of the pull request's existing review, for `review-hog-reviews-get`. Null on the pull request's first run, which creates the review later.
---@field requested_at string Server time when the request was accepted.
---@field resolve_will_run boolean Whether this request plans to run the resolution stage, which can push fix commits to the pull request. It is the plan at request time: a request queued behind a running turn on the same head can be skipped as already published. `review-hog-reviews-pr-status` reports what actually ran.
---@field resolve_skip_reason posthog.review_hog.ResolveSkipReasonEnum|distilled.Null Why the resolution stage does not run: 'run_mode_excludes_resolve' ('review_only' and 'flash' never resolve), 'owner_not_opted_in' (the pull request owner has not turned on resolving comments), 'already_reviewed' (no run starts). Null when it runs. * `run_mode_excludes_resolve` - The run mode never resolves comments * `owner_not_opted_in` - The pull request owner has not opted in to resolution * `already_reviewed` - No run starts, because the head already has a review in this mode

---* `full` - Deep
---* `flash` - Standard
---@alias posthog.review_hog.ReviewTriggerReviewModeEnum "full"|"flash"

---* `pipeline` - Pipeline
---* `single_agent` - Single agent
---@alias posthog.review_hog.ReviewTurnDesignEnum "pipeline"|"single_agent"

---* `flash` - Flash
---* `off` - Off
---@alias posthog.review_hog.ReviewUserRepositoryChoiceModeEnum "flash"|"off"

